      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Computer processing of carotidograms is an incontestable methodical asset. Electronic detection of systolic time intervals excludes human errors, makes possible evaluation of a greater number of systoles, and reduces the effect of nonlinearities of recording. The proposed computerized system saves tedious manual calculations and can yield results with mutual correlations within a short period of time."},
